T{ECB,CBC,CFB64,CFB8,CFB1,OFB}{invperm,permop,subtab,varkey,vartext}.rsp
    NIST CAVP, the known answer tests of the TDES validation system (SP 800-20): the variable plaintext,
    variable key, inverse permutation, permutation operation and substitution table tests, with
    Key1 = Key2 = Key3 (the field KEYs), which is single DES.
    Downloaded from https://csrc.nist.gov/CSRC/media/Projects/Cryptographic-Algorithm-Validation-Program/documents/des/KAT_TDES.zip
    on 2026-10-24.
    License: NIST CAVP test vectors, a work of the United States government (public domain in the United States).
    Used: every record. The pipelined (CFBP) and interleaved (CBCI, OFBI) modes of ANSI X9.52 are not
    implemented, so their files are not included.

T{ECB,CBC,CFB64,CFB8,CFB1,OFB}MMT{2,3}.rsp
    NIST CAVP, the multi-block message tests of TDES with two-key (2) and three-key (3) bundles.
    Downloaded from https://csrc.nist.gov/CSRC/media/Projects/Cryptographic-Algorithm-Validation-Program/documents/des/tdesmmt.zip
    on 2026-10-24.
    License: NIST CAVP test vectors, a work of the United States government (public domain in the United States).
    Used: every record.

T{ECB,CBC}Monte{2,3}.rsp
    NIST CAVP, the Monte Carlo tests of TDES (SP 800-20 tables 6, 12, 18 and 24).
    Downloaded from https://csrc.nist.gov/CSRC/media/Projects/Cryptographic-Algorithm-Validation-Program/documents/des/tdesmct.zip
    on 2026-10-24.
    License: NIST CAVP test vectors, a work of the United States government (public domain in the United States).
    Used: the first records of each direction (each record starts from the keys and the text it lists), and
    the key update of each of them against the keys of the next record; the files set odd parity on the
    updated keys, which DES ignores, so keys are compared without their parity bits.
